I've wondered for a while now what the most possible messages you could
get from quaffing a potion of enlightenment would be. Played around in
wizmode some and I think I may have found the answer. Follow this link
to my copy/paste of the results.

http://filebox.vt.edu/users/nnorman/mostenlightened.txt

To achieve this one must:

*Have obtained all intrinsics possible to get from eating corpses.
*Get crowned.
*Read blessed scroll of food detection or cast food detection.
*Cast detect monsters at skilled or above.
*Read a scroll of confuse monster or cast the spell.
*Quaff a potion of levitation.
*Have the edible rings in your game be: hunger, searching, stealth (can
be obtained through prayer as well), conflict, increase accuracy,
increase damage, regeneration, polymorph, polymorph control and
protection from shapeshifters. Also eat an amulet of restful sleep and
magical breathing. *Be holding a luckstone.
*Buy protection from a priest or get it from prayer or eating ring of
protection.

Equipment: Sting, shield of reflection, fumble gloves, jumping boots,
yellow dragon scale mail, cloak of displacement, cornuthaum (this
character is a wizard), amulet of lifesaving.

Polymorph into a vampire lord (grants flying, the polymorphed line and
level drain resistance while also allows wearing of all armor)

Be riding a mount, then get slimed by a green slime, eat a cockatrice
egg and get engulfed by something. Voila!


As far as I can tell, this is the most lines you could possibly get
from an enlightenment message. I realize that you would get more if
this were your death message (Such as blinded, confused) but that's not
what I'm going for.

There are a few things you could trade around, but I don't think they
would net you any more lines. You could get hallucination resistance
from Grayswandir, or other special artifact messages. You could trade
adornment for free action, and a few other ring effects. You could
trade being mounted for having wounded legs.

Of course, the odds are quite low of all of those rings being edible,
but this is just theoretical. Can anyone think of a combination that
would yield more messages?

And yes, I realize this is pretty useless. =D I found it fun to
experiment though. Hopefully at least one of you will find this as
entertaining as I did.



